Tang-PSX: 32-bit RISC-V (RV32) support for the GNU Lightning RISC-V backend.

Base: third_party/gnu-lightning a6bb2b5 (notaz/gnu_lightning mirror).
Applied by tools/lightning_source.py to an export of that commit; validated
by tests/test_lightning_rv32.py (check suite under qemu-riscv32/64).

- jit_riscv.c: RV32 frame bound, ilp32d double argument passing (register
  pair, a7/stack split, 8-byte aligned stack slots, even pairs for variadic
  doubles), movr_ww_d/movr_d_ww/movi_ww_d emission, 64-bit-only cases and
  the constant pool guarded, 8-byte aligned double callee saves.
- jit_riscv-cpu.c: word-sized ld/st macros, LUI+ADDI constants, word-relative
  extension shifts, word-sized variadic save area.
- jit_riscv-fpu.c: 32-bit int<->FP conversions, double/register-pair moves
  through an allocai'd slot, double constants, aligned va_arg of doubles.
- jit_riscv-sz.c: RV32 instruction-size table.
- jit_fallback.c: little-endian 32-bit unldi_x/unsti_x used the high word as
  the lower-address word of the movr_ww_d/movr_d_ww pair (doc/body.texi).
- lightning.c: without HAVE_MMAP, jit_emit returns NULL when the user code
  buffer is too small, instead of retrying the same emission forever.

This patch is licensed under the GNU LGPL, version 3 or later, as GNU
Lightning is.

